WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.762
This is a short walk-through of the partnership.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:07.227
You will see what you would own, what the clinicians do, and what is handed to you.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:13.418
You will see the platform you would log into, the training, the onboarding, and how patients find your office.

00:00:13.758 --> 00:00:16.358
You do not need a medical background for any of it.

00:00:17.078 --> 00:00:18.524
Let’s start with a question.

00:00:18.864 --> 00:00:25.285
If someone in your town asked you today, “Where can my dad talk to someone about stem cells?” where would you send them?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.400
For most people, there is no number to pass along.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.419
Now imagine being able to say, “Have him call my office. I’ll introduce him to the team.”

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:38.808
That is the kind of business this partnership gives you the opportunity to build.

00:00:39.528 --> 00:00:40.850
Here is who is asking.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:50.335
The Census Bureau counts 61.2 million Americans age 65 and older. That is 13 percent more than in 2020.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:56.323
Older adults now outnumber children in 11 states and in 1,411 counties.

00:00:57.043 --> 00:00:59.109
And here is the market they are part of.

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:07.554
The Global Wellness Institute puts the wellness economy at $7.5 trillion, up 8.9 percent in a single year.

00:01:07.894 --> 00:01:14.185
A large market is not a forecast of what any one office will take in. It tells you the demand is real.

00:01:14.905 --> 00:01:16.822
So what does the partnership give you?

00:01:17.162 --> 00:01:23.741
You build the local business. You open the office, hire a small team and introduce the office to your community.

00:01:24.081 --> 00:01:25.692
People bring you their questions.

00:01:26.032 --> 00:01:33.890
And a licensed clinical team answers the medical ones. A clinician evaluates each person and makes every medical decision.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.494
Here is the same thing as two lists.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:42.304
Yours: the lease, the team, the local advertising, the consultations and the calendar.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:50.185
The clinicians’: evaluating every patient, deciding who is a candidate, choosing the product and performing the procedure.

00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:55.572
You never diagnose anyone, and no medical license is required to own the business.

00:01:56.292 --> 00:02:04.634
Opening an office like this alone takes healthcare attorneys, a supervising physician, a trained clinician and a supplier you can trust.

00:02:04.974 --> 00:02:09.664
A year goes by, and so does a small fortune. Here, all of it is handed to you.

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:16.306
A legal structure for your state, and physician oversight, with your supervising physician named in writing.

00:02:16.646 --> 00:02:21.911
A nurse practitioner for your office, from a staffing network that reaches all 50 states.

00:02:22.251 --> 00:02:27.696
More than 20 biologics at partner pricing, with lot documentation on every order.

00:02:28.036 --> 00:02:33.888
Training for your clinician and your team, and review board training with help enrolling in a registry.

00:02:34.228 --> 00:02:38.618
A pricing playbook, and one named account executive who knows your office.

00:02:39.338 --> 00:02:41.924
Now let me show you the platform you would log into.

00:02:42.264 --> 00:02:47.653
These screens are illustrations, and you will see the real system before you decide anything.

00:02:48.373 --> 00:02:55.025
On your first day, your account executive introduces themselves, and a short checklist shows what to do first.

00:02:55.365 --> 00:02:59.800
Your agreements are signed on the screen, and you can always see how far along you are.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.000
Next comes your website. You choose the name and pick a design.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:10.985
You answer a few questions, and the pages are drafted for you. You can change any word or picture afterward.

00:03:11.325 --> 00:03:16.192
Every office has its own name and its own look, because you are an independent owner.

00:03:16.912 --> 00:03:23.506
Ordering is one screen. You order and reorder at partner pricing, and your order history is one tap away.

00:03:23.846 --> 00:03:26.843
A price sheet with your logo gives you a place to start.

00:03:27.563 --> 00:03:33.867
Then the training. Your clinician gets injection training and coursework, with guided procedure videos.

00:03:34.207 --> 00:03:41.543
You and your team get sales training, scripts and practice conversations, so nobody takes a first consultation cold.

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:50.274
This is the part that brings patients in. An assistant answers your phone, your texts and your website, day and night, within seconds.

00:03:50.614 --> 00:03:53.934
It explains how the office works and books the consultation.

00:03:54.274 --> 00:03:59.895
It gives no medical advice and quotes no prices, and it can pass a caller straight to your team.

00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:07.325
Most people do not book the first time they ask. So the follow-up is drafted for you, by email and by text.

00:04:07.665 --> 00:04:11.882
A built-in check flags wording you should not send, before anything goes out.

00:04:12.602 --> 00:04:18.379
You run the local advertising: the newspaper, the mail and social media, under your own name.

00:04:18.719 --> 00:04:23.449
What you plan to say is reviewed before it runs. No piece promises a result.

00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:31.375
And you can see what the week brought in on one screen: calls, texts, website conversations and consultations booked.

00:04:32.095 --> 00:04:34.160
Two things bring people to your office.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:42.501
The first is regenerative care with biologics, performed by a nurse practitioner at your office under physician oversight.

00:04:42.841 --> 00:04:50.053
The second is the Longevity Chamber™: twelve minutes of full-body red and near-infrared light, offered as a membership.

00:04:50.393 --> 00:04:56.542
It is a general wellness device, not a medical treatment, and it gives patients a reason to come back.

00:04:56.882 --> 00:05:04.251
Every patient is told that the therapies have not been approved by the FDA, and that a clinician decides whether to treat.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:12.650
The minimum investment is $100,000. A local office is required. No medical license is required.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:23.085
Whether it is worth it to you comes down to three numbers: what a patient pays, what the physician and the treatment cost you, and how many patients it takes to cover what you put in.

00:05:23.425 --> 00:05:32.844
Ask us about all three. Financial performance information is provided in the disclosure document, in writing, before you sign or pay anything.

00:05:33.564 --> 00:05:37.826
Here is what happens from here. You read the brief, and we have a thirty-minute call.

00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:39.737
You see the platform itself.

00:05:40.077 --> 00:05:50.883
Then comes the disclosure document: every fee and every obligation, in writing. The law gives you a waiting period, so take it, and hand the document to your attorney.

00:05:51.223 --> 00:05:56.916
After that there is one agreement, and then onboarding, step by step with your account executive.

00:05:57.636 --> 00:06:03.221
Someone in your town is going to ask that question, and somebody’s number is going to get passed along.

00:06:03.561 --> 00:06:05.961
We are placing a limited number of partnerships.

00:06:06.301 --> 00:06:11.412
Ask whether you qualify. It takes about a minute, costs nothing and commits you to nothing.
